# .image-version-ignore — files whose `ghcr.io/vibeic/vibeic-eda:X.Y.Z` mentions
# are HISTORY, not live install pointers, so the drift-net must not flag them
# when VERSION advances. One glob per line (matched against basename AND repo-rel
# path; see sync_image_version.py::_matches). HISTORY_GLOBS already covers
# FIX_STATUS / CHANGELOG / *ROADMAP* / *_STATUS.md.
#
# Benchmark RESULT.md files record WHICH image a PAST clean-room run used (its
# tool-substitution disclosure). That tag is an immutable record of that run —
# never a live pointer that should track VERSION — so ignore them.
RESULT.md
# Sign-off reports are the same: they record the exact toolchain a SPECIFIC
# tapeout/sign-off run used (e.g. a commercial-PDK SPM sign-off on 0.2.16 / yosys 0.66-vibeic).
# 0.2.17 ships yosys 0.67, so bumping the tag would misstate that run — history.
*SIGNOFF*.md

# A benchmark RUN RECORD, not a live install pointer: it states which image
# that run actually used (0.2.20). Rewriting it to the current VERSION would
# falsify the record rather than fix a stale doc — same reason a gatekeeper
# run log is never retroactively edited.
benchmark-data/ic/caravel_user_project/clean_run_v1432int_commercial/SOURCE_MANIFEST.md

# Provenance measurement notes, NOT live install pointers: each records the
# EXACT image the gf180 PDK asset globs were VERIFIED against (0.2.24). The PDK
# assets are identical across EDA-image versions, so the globs stay valid, but
# bumping the tag would FALSELY claim re-verification against a newer image —
# a measurement-honesty violation. Left as the historical 0.2.24 record.
vibe-ic-marketplace/plugins/vibe-ic/programs/pdk_registry.json
vibe-ic-marketplace/plugins/vibe-ic/programs/tests/test_gf180_registry_assets_resolve.py

# Unit-test FIXTURES for the container-image provenance checker. The ghcr tag
# spelled there (0.2.26) is the OLDER image a real container was found to be
# running while 0.2.30 was the intended pin — the measured incident this
# checker exists for. It is not an install pointer: nothing pulls
# (NB: this comment deliberately does NOT spell the full ghcr ref — the
#  drift-net scans this file too, and a ref written here is itself a pointer.)
# it, and it must DIFFER from VERSION or the MISMATCH test stops testing
# anything. Bumping it to the current VERSION would delete the defect the test
# reproduces, which is the opposite of what this drift-net is for.
vibe-ic-marketplace/plugins/vibe-ic/programs/tests/test_container_image_provenance.py

# A PUBLISHED sign-off run record: it states which image regenerated that IR
# result. benchmark-data is read-only to the flow for exactly this reason — the
# tag names the toolchain that produced the numbers beside it, so advancing it
# would attribute those numbers to an image that never ran them.
benchmark-data/ic/spm/v1.5.66_gf180mcuD/reports/phase3/DYNAMIC_IR_REGENERATED.md

# A MEASUREMENT NOTE, not an install pointer. The comment records what `docker
# inspect` actually returned for a named image and docker version, while
# correcting an earlier revision that had asserted the opposite from reasoning.
# The whole value of that note is that it says which image was on the bench; a
# sentence beginning "MEASURED on the image this repo ships" cannot have its
# version advanced without ceasing to be a measurement. The file's OTHER tag
# (the `--require-image` usage example) carries no ghcr prefix and is not a
# pointer this net scans, so ignoring the file costs no live coverage today.
vibe-ic-marketplace/plugins/vibe-ic/programs/container_image_provenance.py
